        <abstract>
          <para>Btrfs subvolumes are separately mountable file hierarchies inside one partition.
        Snapshots are subvolumes that share data with another subvolume. Because Btrfs uses
        copy-on-write, it creates snapshots in seconds and they initially use almost no extra
        disk space. This article explains both concepts, describes how snapshots consume space
        over time and shows how to create, inspect, back up and delete them.</para>
